wayparam (0.6.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release.
  * Add archive-provider abstraction while keeping Wayback as the default.
  * Add Common Crawl CDXJ URL discovery with latest-crawl resolution and
    explicit multi-crawl selection.
  * Add ordered Wayback/Common Crawl collection with cross-provider
    deduplication and source provenance in JSONL.
  * Serialize and rate-limit Common Crawl index requests by default, with a
    descriptive User-Agent and provider-specific filters.
  * Expose archive source selection in the optional local web interface.
  * Keep historical intelligence Wayback-only to avoid ambiguous cross-archive
    capture statistics.

 -- Aleff <alessandro.greco.1@protonmail.com>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 11:47:00 +0200

wayparam (0.5.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release.
  * Add historical endpoint intelligence with first/last seen timestamps,
    capture counts, status-code counts and MIME-type counts.
  * Add historical parameter prevalence and per-domain summary views.
  * Add capture metadata support to the Wayback CDX pagination layer while
    preserving the URL-only iterator contract.
  * Expose historical views in the optional local web interface.
  * Harden target parsing, IPv6 handling, numeric CLI validation and
    cross-platform output filenames.
  * Add Windows/macOS smoke tests and strengthen release artifact checks.

 -- Aleff <alessandro.greco.1@protonmail.com>  Sun, 20 Sep 2026 22:05:20 +0200

wayparam (0.4.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release.
  * Split the optional web interface into the new wayparam-gui package.
  * Fix silent data loss when a result spans several CDX pages: the resumeKey
    walk drops one URL per page boundary while collapse is on. The new default
    (--pagination auto) probes with a single request and switches to the
    lossless block API only when the result really spans pages.
  * Fix --ext-whitelist being cancelled out by the default extension blacklist.
  * Retry truncated CDX responses instead of failing the domain outright.
  * Add --max-results, a global cap so a run can be bounded, and a progress
    line on stderr when it is a terminal.
  * A domain that fails partway through now keeps the stats it earned.
  * Turn malformed input into usage errors instead of tracebacks, in both the
    CLI and the web interface.
  * Cut peak memory on large runs by streaming CDX block pages.

 -- Aleff <alessandro.greco.1@protonmail.com>  Tue, 01 Sep 2026 15:15:15 +0200

